  "patch_scope": "Bazel-compatible core set methods/constructor, assignment-specific mutation, scoped iterator error cleanup and regressions; allocation-free typed BigInt inspection for native JSON preflight; Bazel 9.3 UTF-8 byte-string string methods (ASCII-only case mapping/predicates, ASCII strip whitespace, explicit None strip argument, byte-wise title letter state) and Printer-compatible string repr escaping; location-aware indexing and `in` (StarlarkValue::at_with_location / is_in_with_location with default delegation to at / is_in, used by the ArrayIndex and In bytecode instructions with the expression's lazily computed span) for native ctx.toolchains string keys (docs/TOOLCHAINS.md); Bazel 9.3 StructImpl struct repr (sorted `name = value` fields), BuiltinFunction repr of native functions and bound methods (with an optional builtin receiver for module values such as `native`/`attr`), str()-based `%s`/single-`{}` formatting without `!r`/`!s` conversions (`Missing argument`), `builtin_function_or_method` type (unhashable, as in Bazel) of native functions and bound methods, `<function NAME from FILE>` def/lambda repr, and a `StarlarkValue::collect_debug_print` hook (default `str()`) used by `print`/`fail` (Bazel debugPrint); Bazel's `unhashable type: 'T'` error text; the crate's own tests, doc test, starlark-go testcase and 29 goldens (regenerated with STARLARK_RUST_REGENERATE_GOLDEN_TESTS=1) updated to these behaviours, see BAZEL_RS_MODIFICATIONS.md. Native feature installation remains separate from vendor changes. Bazel 9.3 frozen list/dict mutation text ('trying to mutate a frozen list|dict value', Starlark.checkMutable) and a reverse `|` hook (StarlarkValue::rbit_or) so a dict left operand defers to `select()` (SelectorList.binaryOp with thisLeft = false), also for `|=`. The vendored crate's own frozen list/dict mutation tests and error-display goldens expect that Bazel text (tuples, bytes and sets keep `Immutable`). A value-specific unknown-attribute message hook (StarlarkValue::unknown_attribute_message, default None) used by attribute reads and Value::get_attr_error, for Bazel's ctx.outputs/ctx.executable getErrorMessageForUnknownField texts. N26: Bazel 9.3 string literal values (raw strings keep backslashes; BUILD/.bzl analysis byte escapes decode as UTF-8 with replacement; eval.rs), per-thread Latin-1 char model selection for repository/extension evaluation (values/types/string.rs), split/rsplit with a required string sep, elems() as a list, and Latin-1 isspace/title/capitalize (methods.rs).",
